title: $:/mf/gen/CLI command/mf hash
catalog: CLI command
target: mf hash
summary: Compute the content hashes of the files a query selects

!! Reference

```
Compute the content hashes of the files a query selects

The partial and full hash of each file, with the `stat` stamp they were taken under; a stored hash whose stamp still matches is reused. Files marked `mf_hash` keep theirs fresh on their own; this computes them for any set, now.

Usage: mf hash [OPTIONS] <QUERY>

Arguments:
  <QUERY>
          DSL query selecting the metarecords whose files to hash

Options:
  -s, --simplified
          Treat the query as simplified-language text and expand it first

      --rehash
          Ignore every stored hash and recompute

      --json
          Print the raw JSON summary

      --no-wait
          Print the task id and return instead of waiting

      --poll-interval <MS>
          Milliseconds between task polls

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
```
